{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_nf_witness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_nf_witness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.AbsoluteValue.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.not_atomic_nf_witness_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.not_atomic_nf_witness_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_nf_witness.lean#L136-L145","doc":"**The claim is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is why it is named\nrather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nAt `tr_alt = 0`, `net = 1` the certificate conjunct reads `F_Pauli = 0`, so\n`F_Pauli = 1` fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.groundState_value_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.groundState_value_unique","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_nf_witness.lean#L119-L134","doc":"**The ground-state cost is well defined** — derived.\n\nSub-claim 1 says `π*` is a *global* minimum of `Φ₁`, so any other global\nminimiser has the same cost. This is what \"global minimum\" asserts over and\nabove \"a minimum reached by steepest descent\", and it is the distinction the\n`.md` draws between the exact regime (`C(A,Z) ≤ 50000`) and the descent\nfallback. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.fPauli_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.fPauli_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_nf_witness.lean#L102-L116","doc":"**The Pauli character is non-negative** — derived.\n\n`F_Pauli = |tr_alt/net|` is an absolute value, so `0 ≤ F_Pauli`. Recorded\nbecause it is a property of the certificate that nothing previously checked:\nwith `F_Pauli` a class field, an instance could have supplied a negative one\nand satisfied the carrier only by also choosing `trAlt`/`net` to match. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_nf_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.atomic_nf_witness","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/atomic_nf_witness.lean#L79-L100","doc":"**The claim of `prop:atomic-nf-witness`**, as a proposition over\ncaller-supplied data — sub-claims 1–4 of the `.md`:\n\n1. `π*` globally minimises the nucleon-ordering cost `Φ₁`;\n2. `e*` minimises `Φ₁` over electron positions (the greedy step);\n3. the Gröbner–Shirshov reduction converges at every construction step;\n4. the NF element accumulates without stripping for `A ≤ 9`;\n   and the certificate records `F_Pauli = |tr_alt/net|`.\n\n**Named, not asserted.**  Claim 5 of the `.md` is deliberately absent — see\nthe module docstring: it is a statement about this repository, not about\n`H_{A+Z}(q)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:atomic-nf-witness","label":"prop:atomic-nf-witness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/atomic-nf-witness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}